        ":question/id": "0f081c9f-bb54-5c81-b0a1-377fa45a6087",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x) = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\ln x}$, find $f^{\\prime}(x)$.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}$ and $v(x)=\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}.$\n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})-(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(- \\sin{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})-(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{(\\ln{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{- \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} - \\frac{\\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x}}{\\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}\\\\ &=- \\frac{x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)} \\sin{\\left(x \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(x \\right)}}{x \\ln{\\left(x \\right)}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
